if you pause for a moment and ask  yourself what expectations you have for  the ending of one piece how likely do  you think it is that these expectations  will be fulfilled one piece is without a  doubt an amazing story that has  accompanied many of us for a very long  time yet in the far distance there lurks  a shadow on the horizon that is creeping  near an era with every chapter one sad  day in the hopefully not too close  future the one-piece manga will come to  an end and there will be an epic  showdown long-held mysteries will be  solved dreams fulfilled and everyone  will be happy or will they see the  tricky thing with the long-running  successful fandom is that once they come  to an end more often than not people  seem to be disappointed or even straight  out angry about a particular ending this  can be seen in tv shows like how many  mother in books like harry potter or in  manga as could be seen with naruto while  undoubtedly a lot of people liked the  ending to those particular stories many  if not most fans ended up disappointed  but why does this happen and will one  piece share their fate let's find out  while any story we enjoy brings certain  expectations with it one piece is a  special case in various ways the  one-piece manga has existed for over 20  years now and is still going strong its  continuous success and appeal have many  reasons but three of the story's main  pillars are oda's immense world building  the large and diverse cast of characters  as well as a very straightforward main  character with a very straightforward  goal so it is no wonder that the manga  has recently passed the mark of 450  million sold copies and has thousands of  readers following every new chapter you  could say that one piece is doing as  well as ever but exactly this success is  what has brought an unsatisfactory end  to many other stories the expectation  paradox so what exactly do i mean with  that when i talk about the expectation  paradox i propose that no matter what  the ending of one piece will be like and  no matter how good it will be it will be  disappointing for a huge number of  people in essence one piece cannot have  a great ending from a community  perspective  now why do i make such a ridiculously  sounding claim well mainly there are  three big reasons that make one piece a  top candidate for the expectation  problem and all three of them can be  kind of traced back to its immense  success let's have a look the first  reason is audience diversity oda's story  has accumulated an immense audience that  has been shaped for over more than two  decades one piece is definitely not  simply a story for kids you have young  readers and old readers readers who have  grown up with the story and readers who  just recently discovered it as well as  readers from different cultural  backgrounds while this fact in itself is  simply amazing and speaks for the  greatness of the story it also means  that there exists very different  expectations in the community simply  based on how old you are how long you've  been with the story and what cultural  beliefs and values you have a 15 year  old japanese boy that just started  reading the manga will expect completely  different things from the story than for  example a 28 year old american girl that  has grown up with it both enjoy all the  arcs and the characters and the new  chapters but when it comes to certain  moments and in particular to the ending  both will want completely different  things to happen  one might expect an amazing fight with a  clean happy ending while the other might  want a more serious and subversive or  dramatic ending fact is the audience  diversity of one piece leads to many  people with distinct and specific  expectations for the story's conclusion  the second reason is the incredible  one-piece community and since you're  watching this video right now for better  or worse you're a part of it while i  myself obviously enjoy this community  immensely and love participating in it  it's a big problem in terms of  expectation buildings for fans while  making and watching discussions analysis  and theories of the story are amazingly  fun and in itself is in no term a bad  thing it contributes heavily to people  being dissatisfied with the story going  any other direction than what they  expected and this will be especially the  case once the story wraps up people have  been speculating and theorizing about  the ending of one piece for ages and  have built giant arguments for their  cases seeing these expectations not  fulfilled might make the true ending of  one piece feel disappointing to them the  third reason is pretty much simply time  as mentioned before the manga has  existed for 22 years and even the anime  is celebrating its 20th birthday this  year time does a lot to a story some  people have had years to build their  expectations for certain events others  have changed their taste with the time  and oda himself has shifted his style a  little here and then while a lot of  things happen in the story itself in the  past decades we have heard countless  theories discussions and analysis of  every aspect of one piece to the point  where it sometimes can seem hard to  believe that we haven't heard the true  ending yet somewhere in some long lost  subreddit while the time aspect of one  piece is something i personally more  than love about the manga due to the  years of losing myself in a still  developing world it has set the  expectations for many people in a very  specific direction now those three  reasons the diverse audience the lively  community as well as the time frame of  the story all lead to the conclusion  that it's basically impossible for oda  to write an ending to one piece that  will be seen as great by the majority  this effect will be additionally  strengthened by the nature of ending  itself even if you're happy with the  ending simply the fact that one piece  will be over will add a bit of taste to  it but while it might be inevitable for  a huge part of the community to have  their expectations disappointed in the  end i now want to tell you while you as  an individual should not be afraid of  the final chapter of one piece first of  all you have to find out if you are  someone that tends to have set or  flexible expectations the easiest way  around the expectation paradox in the  first place for you is if you tend to  have a rough idea of what you would like  to see but in general just follow along  with the story and enjoy in whatever  direction it goes if this is the case  for you great you will most likely be  fine since i really do expect oda to  come up with a great ending from a pure  storytelling perspective another type of  person would be someone that has very  set expectations in mind when it comes  to the story wrapping up you expect that  certain things will happen in a certain  way and not differently since that is  how you personally want things to go for  your favorite characters while this is  in no way any better or worse than the  other it is very likely that you will  have a hard time once the last chapter  comes out since the chance of your hat  cannon hitting the jackpot are rather  slim to avoid that it might be worth  trying to go a middle way basically  having certain expectations in mind but  being open for other outcomes as well  that maybe don't fulfill your  expectations but bring closure in a  satisfactory way will it be happy and  heroic will it be dramatic and  subversive or will the ending simply be  a really big plot twist if you follow  one piece until now i'm sure you have  overcome previous expectations before  anyway but most importantly though it  doesn't look like one piece will end  anytime soon so you can simply enjoy  everything around the story for many  more years to come if you want to see  how the expectation paradox plays out  beforehand though you can just come back  to this video later this year after you  watch the final of game of thrones and  then let me know how your experience was  with that ending in any case i  personally am convinced that one piece  will get the ending it deserves i just  hope it will not be over too soon

